<title>JAPAN: Tokyo stock market closed for national holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo stock market closed for national holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo stock market is closed Wednesday for a national holiday. Trade will resume on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Tuesday, the Nikkei 225 closed 25.66 points or 0.14 percent lower at 18,093.13, rescued from an earlier plunge of over 500 points by buying interest in blue-chip issues.</p>
<p>Its March futures closed down 120 points at 18,010.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Equities Desk</p>
</text>
